You're pairing with a developer to author functional contributions for the
Vincia Forge (https://forge.vincia.io). This is the Developer Kit v0.4.0.

Read these before writing code:

1. `README.md` — kit layout + 5 developer tiers
2. `docs/prompt-for-llm.md` — conversational intent-first flow
3. `docs/prompt-for-developer-llm.md` — structural contract, **RULES 1-22**
   (mandatory before any `src/index.ts`)
4. `docs/developer-tiers.md` — 1-page tier summary
5. `docs/blueprint-json-spec.md` — T0 only (`BlueprintDef` field reference)

Pick the closest exemplar before authoring:

- T0 → `examples/blueprint-crm-lite/`, `blueprint-invoicing/`, `blueprint-support-tickets/`
- T1 payment → `examples/connector-stripe-payment/`
- T1 storage → `examples/connector-s3-storage/`
- T1 notification → `examples/connector-slack-notification/`
- T1 auth-provider → `examples/connector-google-auth-provider/`
- T1 mailbox → `examples/connector-sendgrid-mailbox/`
- T2 → `examples/workflow-node-pdf-export/`
- T3 → `examples/widget-stripe-checkout/` (form-aware + cross-tier connector call)
- T4 → `examples/solution-pack-saas-billing/` (manifest-only bundle)

Each example folder has its own `CLAUDE.md` with adaptation notes.

Definition of done:

- `vincia test` passes (vitest)
- `vincia dev` boots cleanly (devcontainer for T1/T2, in-process for T3)
- Manifest passes `vincia:lint_manifest`
- `simulate_run` against fixtures produces expected output (T1/T2)

Visual / template / theme contributions →
[Designer Kit](https://github.com/vincia-io/designer-kit).
